ion Technology Institutional Research, Analytics & Consulting Interactive Media Group International Programs and Off-Campus Study Investments Kent Island Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies Leadership Gifts Library Mathematics McKeen Center for the Common Good Middle Eastern and North African Studies Museum of Art Music Neuroscience Program Outing Club Philosophy Physics and Astronomy President's Office Print Publications & Editorial Services Psychology Quantitative Reasoning Program Registrar Religion Residential & Student Life Romance Languages and Literatures Russian, East European, and Eurasian Studies Safety and Security Schiller Coastal Studies Center Science Center Sociology Special Academic Programs Sponsored Research Stewardship Student Activities Student Aid Student Center for Multicultural Life Student Fellowships/Research THRIVE Test Center Theater and Dance Treasurers Office Upward Bound Womens Resource Center Writing Project Title Schedule No Selection Part Time Year Round Full Time Year Round Full Time Academic Year Part Time Academic Year Casual Adjunct Position Type No Selection Staff Faculty Casual Seasonal Student Previous 1 2 Next View Results (39\n    ) Title Department Position Type Type of Posting Job Close Date Assistant Professor of Mathematics Mathematics Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Mathematics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of assistant professor, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a candidate specializing in probability and stochastic processes, with a preference for those whose scholarship or teaching connects to the mathematics of artificial intelligence and machine learning. The teaching l... View Details Bookmark Budget and Financial Analyst Treasurers Office Staff Internal/External The Budget and Financial Analyst is an integral part of the College’s financial planning and budgeting team, working closely with the Vice President for Finance and Administration and Assistant Treasurer to support the institution’s long-term financial health and strategic goals. The position leads key budgeting, forecasting, financial analysis, and reporting activities, using Workday Financial... View Details Bookmark Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time Safety and Security Casual Internal/External The Casual Parking Enforcement Attendant provides measured enforcement of College parking regulations through the Office of Safety and Security. By following established procedures and employing good common sense, the Parking Enforcement Attendant will work effectively with Safety and Security officers, along with students, faculty, staff, and visitors, contributing to the overall safety of the... View Details Bookmark Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular sta... View Details Bookmark Museum Shop Assistant Museum of Art Casual Internal/External The Museum of Art Shop Assistant will provide consistent and knowledgeable coverage of the pavilion reception area and Museum shop and endorse the programs and mission of the Museum of Art and Bowdoin College. Major responsibilities are to count, greet, and orient visitors to the Museum, be alert to security issues, sell shop merchandise, and answer telephone inquiries. Familiarity with the Mus... View Details Bookmark Outing Club Equipment Room Operations Supervisor Outing Club Casual Internal/External The Bowdoin Outing Club (BOC) Equipment Room outfits over 150 student and staff led outdoor trips annually and offers equipment loans during the academic year for members of the Bowdoin community. The Bowdoin Outing Club Equipment Room Supervisor supports the BOC Director, Associate Director, and Assistant Director in the oversight of the Equipment Room. Specifically, this position directly ove... View Details Bookmark Catering Waitstaff/Bartender (part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.The Catering Waitstaff/Bartender is responsible for wor... View Details Bookmark Cook (late-night shift, part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. We make everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Under the general direction of the Head Chef and Assistant Chefs, we are seeking a p... View Details Bookmark Cook (part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Under the general direction of the Head Chef and Assist... View Details Bookmark Kitchen Assistant - High School Student (part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular sta... View Details Bookmark Food Service Worker (part-time) Dining Service - Thorne Hall Casual Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular sta... View Details Bookmark Cook Dining Service - Smith Union Staff Internal/External Entry level cooking position supporting cooks and chefs. Provides daily food preparation and work environment sanitation. Under supervision of the Lead Cook, prepare daily menu items to recipe specifications.Hourly rate for this position is $21.35/per hourThe schedule for this position is Sunday through Thursday 1pm-9pm during the academic year. Monday through Friday 7am-3pm during the summer, ... View Details Bookmark Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns Development Administration Staff Internal/External In partnership with Lindauer, Bowdoin College is seeking a Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns for its extraordinary Development and Alumni Relations team.Reporting to the Senior Vice President for Development and Alumni Relations, this leader will serveas a strategic advisor, operational partner, and connective force for a division of nearly 60professionals. They wil... View Details Bookmark ​​Events and Special Projects Assistant, President's Office​ President's Office Staff Internal/External The Events and Special Projects Assistant for the President’s Office plans, executes and manages high profile events, projects, and initiatives aligned with Bowdoin College’s strategic goals. The position serves as lead event planner for recurring and ad hoc events and hospitality needs for signature events hosted by the President at Parker Cleaveland House, and locations on and off campus, inc... View Details Bookmark Senior Accountant Controllers Office Staff Internal/External The Senior Accountant has custodial responsibility for capital and non-capital project accounting, including project setup in the ERP system, security access management, funding allocations, and capitalization determinations. This role oversees key plant and project finance processes such as the monthly Plant Funding Analysis, reserve fund reporting, bond requisitions and related funding entrie... View Details Bookmark Security Officer Safety and Security Staff Internal/External The Security Officer provides support through the Campus Communications Center and patrols the College campus on foot, bicycle, or in a security vehicle. The officer is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, alumni, visitors, and property. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to:Conducting daily patrols and walkthroughs of campus bui... View Details Bookmark Procurement & Risk Manager Treasurers Office Staff Internal/External The Procurement & Risk Manager is responsible for managing the College’s property and casualty insurance programs to protect Bowdoin from operating and financial risks, and for providing strategic direction and implementing programs and processes related to College-wide procurement of goods and services. This role serves as a key advisor to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director of Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Management Administration Staff Internal/External The Assistant Director of Environmental Health and Safety will support the Director of Environmental Health and Safety in maintaining Bowdoin College’s comprehensive Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) Program. The Assistant Director will work under the direction of the Director of EHS and be responsible for developing and maintaining safety programs that meet applicable federal, state and lo... View Details Bookmark Kitchen Prep Assistant Dining Service - Thorne Hall Staff Internal/External Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.Bowdoin is seeking a Kitchen Prep Assistant/Production ... View Details Bookmark Laboratory Technician Biology Staff Internal/External A one-year, benefits-eligible position for an NIH-sponsored project on the molecular basis of neuronal regeneration in adult crickets. Responsibilities include: managing the day-to-day operation of the lab (e.g. ordering supplies and equipment, preparing solutions); collaborating with students; and participating significantly in research projects. The position will remain open until a suitable ... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Scholar - Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity Hastings Initiative Staff Internal/External Bowdoin College invites applications for a Hastings Initiative Postdoctoral Scholar beginning September 1, 2026 as part of the Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity. This position offers a unique opportunity for scholars working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and the liberal arts to shape the future of AI engagement in higher education. The appointment will be for two years. T... View Details Bookmark Gift Planning Officer Gift Planning Staff Internal/External The Gift Planning Officer will report to the Director of Gift Planning and work closely with the gift planning team on all aspects of the gift planning program. Responsibilities include: identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of prospective and existing donors, maximizing their annual, capital and planned gifts to the college; establishing long-term relationships with donors... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies (AI) Government Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in comparative public policy or governance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose research involves the law or regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) or the use of AI in policy-making; comparative research across count... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies Government Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the Assistant Professor level in the comparative politics of Africa. The position will begin July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach two courses per semester across a range of offerings, including the department’s introductory course in comparative poli... View Details Bookmark Early Childhood Educator Childrens Center Casual Internal/External The Bowdoin College Children’s Center offers a unique Nature-Based Outdoor Preschool Program that immerses children in the natural world as a central part of their learning experience.Our philosophy is grounded in supporting children’s emotional needs through secure relationships and responsive caregiving. The Children’s Center emphasizes generous amounts of uninterrupted outdoor play, explorat... View Details Bookmark Lecturer in Computer Science Computer Science Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, benefits-eligible lecturer-track position as Lecturer in Computer Science beginning July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for four years, with the potential for recurring multi-year reappointments and eventual promotion to Senior Lecturer, contingent upon successful review and reappointment. The teach... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Cinema Studies Cinema Studies Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Cinema Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Cinema Studies at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and either documentary studies or television studies. Applicants to the documentary track may be scholar-practitioners; applicants to th... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Philosophy Philosophy Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Philosophy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in the philosophy of artificial intelligence (AI) at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is open, with a preference for candidates whose research involves AI related issues in applied ethics or who consider AI from the angle of the philosophy ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Classics Classics Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Classics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in classics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is ancient Mediterranean archaeology, with a preference for candidates whose research involves interactions between Greek, Roman, and other peoples. We welcome interdisciplinary and nontradition... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Dance Theater and Dance Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Theater and Dance invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Dance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is contemporary modern dance with preference given to candidates who also offer an additional technique, especially one that expands our curricular offerings beyond the traditional Euro-Am... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 Next Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
