      "title": "Bowdoin College: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:careers.bowdoin.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Bowdoin College: All Jobs 2026-09-04T13:22:27-04:00 https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18341 2026-09-04T13:22:26-04:00 2026-09-04T13:22:27-04:00 Food Service Worker (part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular staff, we are seeking a <strong>Food Service Worker/Dining Assistant</strong> to join our team. This is a <em>part-time, entry-level</em> role that supports food production and service operations at Bowdoin College’s Dining Halls. Responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Assisting with ingredient preparation for use in recipes for both hot and cold food production, being mindful of cross contamination of foods</li><li>Assisting with servery set-up, service, and replenishment</li><li>Following appropriate food handling and storage procedures; Serve food while adhering to portion control and serving procedures</li><li>Assisting in dishwashing tasks including scraping dirty dishes, loading and unloading pot and dish machine, and stacking clean dishware</li><li>Assisting in sanitation duties including cleaning preparation station and hot line, holding and dispensing equipment, sweeping and mopping kitchen, dining room and service areas, cleaning employee restrooms, wiping walls, tables and chairs, and cleaning all kitchen cooking equipment, refrigerated, frozen and dry storage area, as well as dock area</li><li>Assisting in daily operations and monitoring the dining hall’s checking systems</li><li>Assisting in stocking the gluten-free area and organizing the stocking inventory following FICO standards</li><li>Greeting and assisting dining service patrons</li><li>Providing coverage for the front and back of the house, filling in as needed</li></ul><div><br><em>The hourly rate for this position is $18.40 per hour.<br><br>Shift differentials (2nd shift – 10% shift differential, 3rd shift – 15% shift differential, plus an additional $1.00/hour during weekend working hours).</em></div> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18298 2026-08-28T10:30:24-04:00 2026-08-28T10:30:25-04:00 Lecturer in Computer Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, benefits-eligible lecturer-track position as Lecturer in Computer Science beginning July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for four years, with the potential for recurring multi-year reappointments and eventual promotion to Senior Lecturer, contingent upon successful review and reappointment. The teaching load is five courses per year and is expected to include a regular suite of core introductory-level courses (e.g. <em>Intro to Computer Science, Data Structures</em>) as well as intermediate and advanced courses within the candidate’s area of expertise as opportunity and demand allow. As the primary focus for lecturer-track faculty is on teaching and pedagogy, the successful candidate will have a demonstrated history of pedagogical innovation and a commitment to keep abreast of advances in computer science pedagogy. An advanced degree (master’s or doctorate) in Computer Science or a related field is expected by the date of appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching. The College offers opportunities for professional development, including a path to promotion to senior lecturer and eligibility for fully funded, one-semester senior lecturer sabbatical leaves, as well as support for teaching, grant-writing, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty, and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 4) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin<strong> January 19, 2027</strong>, and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment without prior lecturer-track experience is $94,000 - $100,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Computer Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18343 2026-09-04T13:23:22-04:00 2026-09-04T13:23:23-04:00 Cook (part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Under the general direction of the Head Chef and Assistant Chefs, we are seeking a part-time Cook to provide support in food preparation for catering and hot and cold food production, while maintaining a clean and sanitary work space. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Assembling and cooking recipes for daily menus</li><li>Preparation of ingredients in recipes for both hot and cold food production</li><li>Assisting with catering function set-ups and preparation</li><li>Assisting with position coverage in production and service areas as required</li><li>Operating cold food prep and short-order cooking equipment</li><li>Maintaining workspace in a clean and sanitary manner</li><li>Reading recipes and preparing to specifications</li></ul><div><em><br>The hourly pay for this position is $21.00 per hour.<br><br>Shift differentials (2nd shift – 10% shift differential, 3rd shift – 15% shift differential, plus an additional $1.00/hour during weekend working hours).</em></div> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18327 2026-09-03T15:17:05-04:00 2026-09-03T15:17:06-04:00 Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the Assistant Professor level in the comparative politics of Africa. The position will begin July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach two courses per semester across a range of offerings, including the department’s introductory course in comparative politics, taught in rotation. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in political science is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create inclusive learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 4) a writing sample; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 21 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.</div><div><br>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Government https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18087 2026-07-27T14:53:41-04:00 2026-07-27T14:53:41-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor of Education <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Education invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Education beginning July 1, 2027. Applicants at the Assistant and Associate level are encouraged to apply. The position subfield is open with a preference for candidates with a background in mathematics or data science and whose research involves Learning Sciences with a distinct focus on the development and role of artificial intelligence (AI) in teaching and learning. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in Education or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s Department of Education houses the <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/education/teacher-scholars/index.html\"><strong>Bowdoin Teacher Scholars</strong></a> (BTS) program that offers both current students and recent graduates the opportunity to become certified public school teachers. This hire will work in collaboration with current Education faculty to revise courses for the BTS pathway to include content related to AI.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.</div><div><br>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references of candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually and at the associate professor rank is $120,000 - $140,000. The salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu.</strong></a></div> Education https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18345 2026-09-04T13:24:27-04:00 2026-09-04T13:24:27-04:00 Catering Waitstaff/Bartender (part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>The Catering Waitstaff/Bartender is responsible for working various events on campus following standard procedures to facilitate service of food and beverages to Bowdoin College catering customers.<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Compensation and Perks:</strong><ul><li>The hourly rate for this position is $23.50 per hour, and this position is eligible for overtime, shift, and weekend pay differentials</li><li>Shift Differentials: 10% for 2nd shift, 15% for 3rd shift, plus an additional $1.00/hour for weekend hours</li><li>Employees are guaranteed a minimum of 3 hours of pay when scheduled to work</li><li>Employees are provided a free meal on scheduled workdays</li><li><br></li></ul></li></ul> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18330 2026-09-04T13:11:50-04:00 2026-09-04T13:11:50-04:00 Gift Planning Officer <div>The Gift Planning Officer will report to the Director of Gift Planning and work closely with the gift planning team on all aspects of the gift planning program. Responsibilities include: identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of prospective and existing donors, maximizing their annual, capital and planned gifts to the college; establishing long-term relationships with donors; marketing and communications; event and meeting planning; internal and external administrative duties; working in collaboration with other offices of development and relationship managers to meet Bowdoin's fundraising objectives.<br><br>Essential Functions:<br><br></div><ul><li>Initiates and executes development strategies for alumni, parents, and friends to secure support through comprehensive gift plans including, but not limited to, gifts of: bequests and beneficiary designations; life-income vehicles; real estate; personal property; life insurance; closely held stock; gifts-in-kind; as well as outright gifts of cash and stock.</li><li>As a frontline fundraiser, develops, solicits, and stewards a personal caseload of approximately 120 prospects, and establishes and maintains long-term donor relationships with the College. Frequent travel to engage prospective and current donors in their comprehensive support of the College through annual, capital, and planned gifts.</li><li>Collaborates with the gift planning and communications teams in an annual strategic marketing and stewardship plan for the purposes of educating constituents about gift planning and growing membership in the Bowdoin Pines Society.</li><li>Develops and maintains technical expertise and knowledge of complex planned gifts and applies this expertise with donors and their advisers.</li></ul><div><br>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $107,500 - 117,500 annually.<br><br><br></div><div>BENEFITS AND PERKS</div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Gift Planning https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18347 2026-09-04T13:25:27-04:00 2026-09-04T13:25:27-04:00 Museum Shop Assistant <div>The Museum of Art Shop Assistant will provide consistent and knowledgeable coverage of the pavilion reception area and Museum shop and endorse the programs and mission of the Museum of Art and Bowdoin College. Major responsibilities are to count, greet, and orient visitors to the Museum, be alert to security issues, sell shop merchandise, and answer telephone inquiries. Familiarity with the Museum’s current temporary exhibitions and permanent collections is important. This position may also provide support to the shop manager by helping to receive merchandise and restock.<br><br>The hourly range for this position is expected to be: $18.00/hr</div> Museum of Art https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18104 2026-07-28T14:30:56-04:00 2026-07-28T14:30:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Computer Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Computer Science at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose research involves artificial intelligence (AI) or interdisciplinary work involving AI. We especially encourage those whose work intersects with trustworthy AI (e.g., explainability, interpretability, or privacy in AI models) or natural language processing (NLP) to apply. The teaching load is two courses per semester. This hire will teach at all levels of the Computer Science curriculum, including introductory courses as well as advanced courses within the candidate's area of expertise.&nbsp; Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this position, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of your plans for research 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Review of applications will begin October 1 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $122,000 - $128,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Computer Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18332 2026-09-04T13:13:15-04:00 2026-09-04T13:13:15-04:00 Laboratory Technician <div>A one-year, benefits-eligible position for an NIH-sponsored project on the molecular basis of neuronal regeneration in adult crickets. Responsibilities include: managing the day-to-day operation of the lab (e.g. ordering supplies and equipment, preparing solutions); collaborating with students; and participating significantly in research projects. The position will remain open until a suitable candidate is identified.<br><br>The hourly range for this position is expected to be: $26.85-28.30/per hour<br><br><strong>BENEFITS AND PERKS</strong></div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical – effective date of hire, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 10.12% annual compensation contribution (Eligible after 1 year of service and age 26), no match or vesting required!</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 10 days of vacation (1st year), 15 days (2nd year), 12 days of personal/sick time (PTO accruals based on hours worked).</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool (Including household members)</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Biology https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18349 2026-09-04T13:26:13-04:00 2026-09-04T13:26:13-04:00 Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time <div>The Casual Parking Enforcement Attendant provides measured enforcement of College parking regulations through the Office of Safety and Security. By following established procedures and employing good common sense, the Parking Enforcement Attendant will work effectively with Safety and Security officers, along with students, faculty, staff, and visitors, contributing to the overall safety of the Campus.<br><br></div><div><strong>Essential Functions:</strong></div><ul><li>Acquire and maintain a thorough knowledge of the college campus and layout of streets, buildings, and other significant areas of the college campus so as to maximize the accuracy of documentation.</li><li>Be thoroughly familiar with the Department of Safety and Security’s organizational philosophy.</li><li>Assist in ensuring good public relations between the College and local communities, and provide general assistance to all persons on the campus including information regarding campus locations, special events, and campus regulations.</li><li>Identify vehicles in violation of parking regulations, checking with Safety and Security Communications, when necessary, to confirm vehicle and owner information before issuing parking violations or warnings.</li><li>Relay information to Safety and Security Communications relating to incidents or emergencies, using two-way radios or cell phone.</li><li>Observe and report hazardous conditions such as malfunctioning traffic signals, missing signs, and the absence of parking and street markings.</li></ul><div><br><strong>The hourly rate for this position is $18.40 per hour.</strong></div> Safety and Security https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18108 2026-07-28T14:42:26-04:00 2026-07-28T14:42:26-04:00 Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Earth and Oceanographic Science invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in geoscience applications of artificial intelligence at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose scholarship critically examines, thoughtfully utilizes, or ethically guides AI to advance understanding of geoscience processes. Areas of geoscience expertise might include glacial geology/geomorphology, glaciology, geophysics, neotectonics, sedimentology, stratigraphy, tectonic geomorphology, or atmospheric science, with a preference for those whose work intersects with surface earth processes and focuses on thousand- to million-year timescales. These fields and timescales have critical intersections with and implications for how humans live on and with Earth, even as the landscape and climate change in response to both natural and human activities. These areas of geoscience expertise also align with the EOS Department's earth system science approach to investigating fundamental questions about Earth’s past, present, and future.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will teach three courses per year, including two courses with separate lab sections. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term, successful scholarship and who will offer opportunities to engage students in research. A Ph.D. in geoscience or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this one, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>The College’s location along the rocky Maine coast provides excellent local field sites for teaching and research. Bowdoin maintains a High Performance Computer (HPC) cluster and access to GIS software. Department facilities include mineral, rock, and fossil collections; augmented reality sandbox; stream table; rock saws; shallow water current meters; remote water samplers for river analysis; ACDP; petrographic microscopes; and SEM (Scanning Electron Microscope) with CL/EDS/EBSD capabilities. For more information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/earth-oceanographicscience/\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/earth-oceanographicscience/</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Pleasesubmit the following: (1) a one-page cover letter; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a three-page statement that describes your teaching practices, including a description of courses you would be interested in teaching that would enrich existing curriculum in EOS (<a href=\"https://bowdoin-public.courseleaf.com/courses/eos/\"><strong>https://bowdoin-public.courseleaf.com/courses/eos/</strong></a>); (4) a two-page research statement; (5) a one-page statement that describes your philosophy and use of AI; and (6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references for candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 1, 2026,</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Earth and Oceanographic Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18334 2026-09-04T13:14:25-04:00 2026-09-04T13:14:25-04:00 Assistant Director of Environmental Health and Safety <div>The Assistant Director of Environmental Health and Safety will support the Director of Environmental Health and Safety in maintaining Bowdoin College’s comprehensive Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) Program. The Assistant Director will work under the direction of the Director of EHS and be responsible for developing and maintaining safety programs that meet applicable federal, state and local regulations and standards. This position provides campus outreach, communications and education across academic and administrative departments that promote risk reduction and awareness of EHS issues. Additional responsibilities include ongoing development and management of the campus learning management system to support all EHS related training programs. The Assistant Director supervises one Safety Specialist.<br><br></div><div><strong>COMPENSATION</strong></div><ul><li>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $77,200-$84,100.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS AND PERKS</strong></div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Facilities Management Administration https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18351 2026-09-04T15:33:51-04:00 2026-09-04T15:33:51-04:00 Assistant Professor of Mathematics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Mathematics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of assistant professor, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a candidate specializing in probability and stochastic processes, with a preference for those whose scholarship or teaching connects to the mathematics of artificial intelligence and machine learning. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in mathematics, applied mathematics, or statistics is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.</div><div><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.</div><div><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions through MathJobs (<a href=\"https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670</strong></a>). A complete application includes:</div><ul><li>a cover letter of up to two pages describing your experience and your short- and long-term goals in teaching and research. In your letter, please give specific examples of how your scholarship or teaching has engaged meaningfully with the mathematics underlying machine learning or AI – for example, stochastic optimization and sampling algorithms, high dimensional probability, diffusion models, statistical learning theory or teaching courses on the mathematical foundations of ML;</li><li>a curriculum vitae;</li><li>a research statement;</li><li>a teaching statement describing your pedagocial experience and your approach to engaging and supporting students from a broad range of backgrounds;</li><li>three letters of reference: two addressing research and one addressing teaching, submitted directly by the letter writers through MathJobs.</li></ul><div><br>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 8</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000-$98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.</div><div><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Mathematics https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18112 2026-07-28T14:51:13-04:00 2026-07-28T14:51:14-04:00 Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Environmental Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in environmental humanities at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The humanities field is open and we welcome candidates who bring diverse humanistic perspectives to environmental inquiry, but excludes history for which expertise already exists in the program. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with the promise of long-term successful research and/or creative work. The successful candidate will teach four courses per year, including a rotating teaching responsibility for an introductory interdisciplinary environmental studies course, an intermediate-level humanities core course and an advanced-level capstone for environmental studies majors, and courses in the environmental humanities informed by the candidate’s area(s) of expertise. The successful candidate also is expected to direct student research.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research and/or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Environmental Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18336 2026-09-04T13:15:16-04:00 2026-09-04T13:15:17-04:00 Security Officer <div>The Security Officer provides support through the Campus Communications Center and patrols the College campus on foot, bicycle, or in a security vehicle. The officer is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, alumni, visitors, and property. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conducting daily patrols and walkthroughs of campus buildings and grounds, including locking and unlocking buildings and inspecting fire and access control alarm systems</li><li>Monitoring the condition of campus buildings and taking steps to prevent damage or theft, as well as identifying and reporting hazards such as broken lights or unsafe conditions during patrols</li><li>Investigating incidents, crimes, and complaints involving the College or its community members, and ensuring compliance with established regulations and policies</li><li>Operating the Campus Security Communications Center by monitoring alarms, responding to complaints and requests, and coordinating response efforts by communicating with patrol officers via radio or other means</li><li>Maintaining detailed and accurate records as it pertains to incidents, activities, and communications</li><li>While this is a fairly entry-level position, Bowdoin will provide 5 weeks of training to new security employees, further training at 6 months, and offer other opportunities for training through out the year such as deescalation trainings.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Schedule:</strong></div><ul><li><strong>This position is full time, year round, 40 hours per week (1.0 FTE). 7 am - 3:00 pm Friday through Monday with Tuesdays and Wednesdays off.</strong></li></ul><div><br><strong>Compensation:</strong></div><ul><li>The hourly rate for this position is $21.35 per hour. Exact compensation will be determined based on years of applicable experience.</li><li>This position is eligible for overtime and a weekend differential.</li><li>2nd Shift Differential (10%): Applies to hours Worked from 3:00 p.m. to 11:00 p.m.</li><li>3rd Shift Differential (15%): Applies to hours worked from 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m.<ul><li>$21.35 × 15% = $3.20 additional per hour</li></ul></li><li>Weekend Differential: Additional $1.00 per hour for hours worked on Saturday and Sunday.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Benefits and Perks:</strong></div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 10.12% of annual compensation contribution (Eligible after 1 year of service and age 26), no match or vesting required!</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 10 days of vacation (1st year), 15 days (2nd year), 12 days of personal/sick time (PTO accruals based on hours worked).</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off</li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool (Including household members)</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Safety and Security https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18258 2026-08-20T09:37:34-04:00 2026-08-20T09:37:35-04:00 Cleaner <div>The Cleaner I is responsible for maintaining the cleanliness and condition standards of the College’s buildings and immediate grounds. The Cleaner I performs a variety of housekeeping duties to maintain cleanliness and hygiene standards in both residential and administrative settings. This entry-level position involves routine cleaning tasks and requires attention to detail and the ability to work efficiently to ensure a clean and safe environment for residents or occupants.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Perform general cleaning tasks, including dusting, sweeping, mopping, and vacuuming floors.</li><li>Clean and sanitize bathrooms, including toilets, sinks, showers, and countertops.</li><li>Clean and disinfect kitchen areas, including countertops, appliances, and sinks.</li><li>Empty trash receptacles and dispose of waste in accordance with established procedures.</li><li>Clean and polish mirrors, glass surfaces, and windows as needed.</li><li>Replenish cleaning supplies and notify supervisor of any shortages or equipment malfunctions.</li><li>Follow established cleaning schedules and procedures to ensure consistency and efficiency.</li><li>Report any maintenance issues or safety hazards to the supervisor promptly.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Compensation:</strong></div><ul><li>Hourly rate for this position is $19.00 per hour (this role is eligible for overtime and shift differentials)</li></ul><div><strong><br>Benefits and Perks:</strong></div><ul><li>Medical Insurance (Effective on date of hire)</li><li>Vision and Dental Insurance</li><li>Life Insurance and Disability Insurance</li><li>$1,000 Employee Referral Program Bonus</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 10.12% annual compensation contribution (Eligible after 1 year of service and age 26 )</li><li>Accrue up to 10 day of vacation (1st year), 15 days (2nd year)</li><li>Accrue up to 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays</li><li>Paid Parental Leave (After 1 year)</li><li>Access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool (Including household)</li><li>Free wellness classes</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> FM - Housekeeping https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18338 2026-09-04T13:20:44-04:00 2026-09-04T13:20:45-04:00 ​​Events and Special Projects Assistant, President's Office​ <div>The Events and Special Projects Assistant for the President’s Office plans, executes and manages high profile events, projects, and initiatives aligned with Bowdoin College’s strategic goals. The position serves as lead event planner for recurring and ad hoc events and hospitality needs for signature events hosted by the President at Parker Cleaveland House, and locations on and off campus, including but not limited to Board of Trustee meetings, meals and events with internal and external stakeholders, and other major ceremonies and milestones.<br><br></div><div>The role requires close coordination with President’s Office team staff, Cleaveland House manager, academic departments and administrative offices to ensure the flawless execution of time-sensitive, high-visibility events. In addition, this position provides broader special-projects and administrative support that advances Bowdoin College’s strategic priorities.<br><br>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS</div><ul><li>Working closely with members of the President’s Office team, design, plan, execute and staff the President’s recurring calendar of signature events, as well as non-recurring meals and special occasions hosted by the President at Parker Cleaveland House.</li><li>Design, plan, execute and staff the Commencement dinner for honorary degree recipients and serve as primary point of contact for the College’s honorary degree recipients leading up to and through Commencement weekend, coordinating all visit logistics.</li><li>​​Working closely with the President’s Office staff and the Secretary of the College, lead on the hospitality elements of Board of Trustee meetings, including all meals, receptions, and refreshments.</li><li>​Provide comprehensive logistical and operational support for special meetings, retreats, or campus events associated with Presidential projects, and other high-level institutional visits. Support includes planning and execution of schedule, ​​receptions and meals, and involves close coordination with campus constituents and external stakeholders.</li><li>Provide scheduling, invoicing, and general administrative support for special projects and initiatives within the President’s Office, including backup sick/vacation coverage for the EA roles in the office, as needed.</li><li>Maintain detailed and organized records, documentation, and reference materials. Conduct post-event debrief, and follow-up; preserve institutional knowledge and find opportunities for creativity and innovation to improve execution of recurring events year over year.</li></ul><div><br>This position is scheduled for 24 hours per week.<br>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $$40,600 - 43,800 annually.<br><br>BENEFITS AND PERKS</div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Paid Time Off: vacation and personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul><div><br></div> President's Office https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18279 2026-08-25T09:24:55-04:00 2026-08-25T09:24:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Classics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Classics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in classics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is ancient Mediterranean archaeology, with a preference for candidates whose research involves interactions between Greek, Roman, and other peoples. We welcome interdisciplinary and nontraditional approaches to the study of classics. The teaching load is two courses per semester; successful candidates will contribute enthusiastically to the department’s Latin, Greek and Classics course offerings. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in classics, archaeology, or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 25, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Classics https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18340 2026-09-04T13:21:50-04:00 2026-09-04T13:21:50-04:00 Cook <div>Entry level cooking position supporting cooks and chefs. Provides daily food preparation and work environment sanitation. Under supervision of the Lead Cook, prepare daily menu items to recipe specifications.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Hourly rate for this position is $21.35/per hour</li><li>The schedule for this position is Sunday through Thursday 1pm-9pm during the academic year. Monday through Friday 7am-3pm during the summer, winter break and spring break.</li></ul><div><br><strong>BENEFITS AND PERKS</strong></div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical – effective date of hire, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 10.12% annual compensation contribution (Eligible after 1 year of service and age 26), no match or vesting required!</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 10 days of vacation (1st year), 15 days (2nd year), 12 days of personal/sick time (PTO accruals based on hours worked).</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool (Including household members)</li></ul> Dining Service - Smith Union https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18289 2026-08-26T09:53:43-04:00 2026-08-26T09:53:44-04:00 Assistant Professor of Cinema Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Cinema Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Cinema Studies at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and either documentary studies or television studies. Applicants to the documentary track may be scholar-practitioners; applicants to the television track may have a primarily scholarly focus. In either case, we welcome research examining AI’s social, political, aesthetic, economic, or ethical dimensions within the relevant field. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research or creative work. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines, including this position; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission. computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 5) a sample of scholarly work no longer than 20 pages; 6) if relevant, a film or other creative work of no more than 20 minutes’ duration accompanied by a creator’s statement of no more than 500 words, made accessible via a link (including a password, if desired) embedded in the candidate’s cover letter; and 7) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 4, 2026 </strong>and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Cinema Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18342 2026-09-04T13:22:54-04:00 2026-09-04T13:22:55-04:00 Kitchen Assistant - High School Student (part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular staff, we are seeking a <strong>Kitchen Assistant/Dining Hall Assistant</strong> to join our team. This is a <em>part-time, entry-level</em> role that supports food production and service operations at Bowdoin College’s Dining Halls. Responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Assisting with ingredient preparation for use in recipes for both hot and cold food production, being mindful of cross contamination of foods</li><li>Assisting with servery set-up, service, and replenishment</li><li>Following appropriate food prepping, handling and storage procedures; Preparing food as a display or egg cook; Serving food while adhering to portion control and serving procedures</li><li>Assisting in dishwashing tasks including scraping dirty dishes, loading and unloading pot and dish machine, and stacking clean dishware</li><li>Assisting in sanitation duties including cleaning preparation station and hot line, holding and dispensing equipment, sweeping and mopping kitchen, dining room and service area, and wiping walls, tables and chairs</li><li>Greeting and assisting dining service patrons</li><li>Providing coverage for the front and back of the house, filling in as needed</li></ul><div><br><em>The hourly rate for this position is $16.80 per hour.<br><br>Shift differentials (2nd shift – 10% shift differential, 3rd shift – 15% shift differential, plus an additional $1.00/hour during weekend working hours).</em></div> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18325 2026-09-03T11:39:17-04:00 2026-09-03T11:39:17-04:00 Early Childhood Educator <div>The <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/childrens-center/\"><strong>Bowdoin College Children’s Center </strong></a>offers a unique Nature-Based Outdoor Preschool Program that immerses children in the natural world as a central part of their learning experience.<br><br>Our <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/childrens-center/index.html\"><strong>philosophy</strong></a> is grounded in supporting children’s emotional needs through secure relationships and responsive caregiving. The Children's Center emphasizes generous amounts of uninterrupted outdoor play, exploration, and experimentation as key components of our nature-based curriculum. We are an NAEYC-accredited program deeply engaged in anti-bias and anti-racist work, supported by professional development and ongoing consultation throughout the year.</div><div><br>We are seeking an <strong>Early Childhood Educator</strong> to join our collaborative and professional team. This role offers a dynamic opportunity to work in a college campus-based childcare center committed to providing high-quality care and education. The Children’s Center fosters a calm, organized, and engaged work environment where staff collaborate weekly to reflect on practices, discuss concerns, and plan curriculum. The Early Childhood Educator plays a vital support role in ensuring the smooth daily operations of the program. Responsibilities may include:</div><ul><li>Assisting with supervision both indoors and outdoors</li><li>Supporting daily routines such as setting up nap time, prepping snacks, and washing dishes</li><li>Reading stories, singing songs, and engaging meaningfully with children</li><li>Participating in the classroom in alignment with the Center’s mission and philosophy</li></ul><div>This is an excellent opportunity for those interested in early childhood education and exploring career paths in childcare. Many of our full-time staff began as part-time Educators.</div><div><br><em>The hourly rate for this position is $21 per hour.<br>This is a part time \"casual\" position, meaning a schedule of up to 19 hours per week.</em></div> Childrens Center https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18344 2026-09-04T13:23:54-04:00 2026-09-04T13:23:55-04:00 Cook (late-night shift, part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. We make everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining</em>! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Under the general direction of the Head Chef and Assistant Chefs, we are seeking a part-time, <strong>late-night Cook </strong>to support our <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/news/2019/10/between-the-bells-supersnack.html\"><strong>SuperSnack</strong></a> operation at Thorne Dining Hall. SuperSnack is a highly popular, late-night dining service for students. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Assembling and cooking recipes for daily menus</li><li>Preparation of ingredients in recipes for both hot and cold food production</li><li>Assisting with catering function set-ups and preparation</li><li>Assisting with position coverage in production and service areas as required</li><li>Operating cold food prep and short-order cooking equipment</li><li>Maintaining workspace in a clean and sanitary manner</li><li>Reading recipes and preparing to specifications</li></ul><div><br><strong>Compensation:</strong></div><ul><li>The hourly rate for this position is $21.00 per hour</li><li>10% Shift Differential for hours worked from 3:00 pm to 11:00 pm</li><li>15% Shift Differential for hours worked from 11:00 pm to 2:00 am</li><li>Supersnack Premium of an additional $4.00 per hour for hours worked from 10:00 pm to 2:00 am</li><li>Weekend Differential of an additional $1.00 per hour for hours worked on Saturday and Sunday</li></ul> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18328 2026-09-03T15:17:31-04:00 2026-09-03T15:17:31-04:00 Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies (AI) <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in comparative public policy or governance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose research involves the law or regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) or the use of AI in policy-making; comparative research across countries or policy areas is a plus. The successful candidate will teach two courses per semester across a range of offerings, including participation in the rotation of the department’s introductory course in comparative politics or international relations. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in political science or related fields is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions – including this position - across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create inclusive learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 4) a writing sample; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 21, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<strong><br></strong><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Government https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18102 2026-07-28T14:16:45-04:00 2026-07-28T14:16:46-04:00 Assistant Professor of Asian Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Asian Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Chinese language, literature and culture at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The area of specialization is open. The teaching load is two courses per semester including both language courses and thematic courses taught in English. The successful candidate will be integral in the Chinese language program, participating fully in the language program activities and teaching one to two courses in Chinese each year. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. Candidates must have native or near-native fluency in Mandarin and training in Chinese language pedagogy. A Ph.D is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and from those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College:<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 1, 2026 </strong>and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Asian Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18346 2026-09-04T13:24:59-04:00 2026-09-04T13:25:00-04:00 Outing Club Equipment Room Operations Supervisor <div>The Bowdoin Outing Club (BOC) Equipment Room outfits over 150 student and staff led outdoor trips annually and offers equipment loans during the academic year for members of the Bowdoin community. The Bowdoin Outing Club Equipment Room Supervisor supports the BOC Director, Associate Director, and Assistant Director in the oversight of the Equipment Room. Specifically, this position directly oversees student employees during their gear room shift, providing the vision for daily workflow, task delegation, and instruction in gear repair. Additionally, this position works closely with the BOC Director to monitor equipment inventory, track equipment use and order replacements based on lifecycle, use, and anticipated program changes. This position will oversee the outfitting and de-issue process for weekly trips, Orientation Trips and complete other projects as assigned related to improving gear room operations. Lastly, the supervisor will be instrumental in prepping equipment for the upcoming season as well as repairing gear to return it to circulation when appropriate.<br><br><strong>COMPENSATION:</strong></div><ul><li>The hourly range for this position is expected to be: $21.00/per hour</li><li>This is a casual, part-time, non-benefit eligible position working less than 19 hours/week for the academic year</li></ul><div><br></div> Outing Club https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18331 2026-09-04T13:12:31-04:00 2026-09-04T13:12:32-04:00 Postdoctoral Scholar - Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity <div>Bowdoin College invites applications for a Hastings Initiative Postdoctoral Scholar beginning September 1, 2026 as part of <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>the Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a>. This position offers a unique opportunity for scholars working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and the liberal arts to shape the future of AI engagement in higher education. The appointment will be for two years. The ideal candidates will have a demonstrated commitment to integrating AI in their scholarship and instruction and may come from any discipline. A PhD is expected prior to the start date.<br><br></div><div>The Postdoctoral Scholar will serve as one of the Initiative’s AI specialists, helping to shape the College's approach to AI integration while maintaining its liberal arts values.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities</strong> <strong>include</strong>:</div><ul><li>Collaborating with and supporting Bowdoin faculty in integrating AI tools and methodologies into their teaching and research. This work will include:</li><li>Offering one-on-one consultations, which may develop into longer-term research collaborations, including substantive and potentially coauthored scholarship</li><li>Envisioning, planning, and running workshops and symposia with support from the Hastings Advisory Committee and Post-baccalaureate Fellows in AI and Humanity</li><li>Teaching in the planned workshops</li><li>Actively promoting the ethical use of AI beyond the Bowdoin community through scholarly output and activities, including participation in conferences, workshops, and other outreach initiatives.</li><li>Working with the Hastings Advisory Committee to further develop the Initiative.</li><li>Supporting the Initiative’s Director in administrating the Initiative</li><li>Developing the Scholar’s own research program</li></ul><div><br><strong>COMPENSATION</strong></div><ul><li>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $78,000-$83,000</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS AND PERKS</strong></div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Hastings Initiative https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18348 2026-09-04T13:25:49-04:00 2026-09-04T13:25:50-04:00 Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time) <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular staff, we are seeking a part-time, entry-level <strong>Food Service Worker/Dining Assistant</strong> to support our <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/news/2019/10/between-the-bells-supersnack.html\"><strong>SuperSnack</strong></a> operation at Thorne Dining Hall. SuperSnack is a highly popular, late-night dining service for students.<br>Responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Assisting with ingredient preparation for use in recipes for both hot and cold food production, being mindful of cross contamination of foods</li><li>Assisting with servery set-up, service, and replenishment</li><li>Following appropriate food handling and storage procedures; Serve food while adhering to portion control and serving procedures</li><li>Assisting in dishwashing tasks including scraping dirty dishes, loading and unloading pot and dish machine, and stacking clean dishware</li><li>Assisting in sanitation duties including cleaning preparation station and hot line, holding and dispensing equipment, sweeping and mopping kitchen, dining room and service areas, cleaning employee restrooms, wiping walls, tables and chairs, and cleaning all kitchen cooking equipment, refrigerated, frozen and dry storage area, as well as dock area</li><li>Assisting in daily operations and monitoring the dining hall’s checking systems</li><li>Assisting in stocking the gluten-free area and organizing the stocking inventory following FICO standards</li><li>Greeting and assisting dining service patrons</li><li>Verifying student identification/board eligibility for specific meals and verifying meal counts</li><li>Providing coverage for the front and back of the house, filling in as needed</li></ul><div><br><strong>Compensation:</strong></div><ul><li>The hourly rate for this position is $18.40 per hour</li><li>10% Shift Differential for hours worked from 3:00 pm to 11:00 pm</li><li>15% Shift Differential for hours worked from 11:00 pm to 2:00 am</li><li>Supersnack Premium of an additional $4.00 per hour for hours worked from 10:00 pm to 2:00 am</li><li>Weekend Differential of an additional $1.00 per hour for hours worked on Saturday and Sunday</li></ul> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18107 2026-07-28T14:39:02-04:00 2026-07-28T14:39:02-04:00 Assistant Professor of English (Creative Writing) <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of English invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in creative writing at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The subfields for this position are poetry and fiction, with a primary specialization in poetry and a secondary specialization in fiction. Successful candidates will have a strong record of publication and teaching in both subfields. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful creative work. An MFA, Ph.D., or equivalent terminal graduate degree in creative writing or a related discipline is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 5) a writing sample of no more than 50 pages total that includes both fiction and poetry and 6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin Friday, <strong>September 18</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> English https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18333 2026-09-04T13:13:45-04:00 2026-09-04T13:13:46-04:00 Kitchen Prep Assistant <div>Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently <em>rated in the top 10 for college dining!</em> We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations.<br><br>Bowdoin is seeking a <strong>Kitchen Prep Assistant/Production Assistant </strong>to join our team at Thorne Hall.<br><br>Under supervision of the Head Chef, Assistant Chef/Cold Food Production Coordinator, with guidance from Production Assistant Lead, the <strong>Kitchen Prep Assistant/Production Assistant </strong>is responsible for preparation of daily cold food items to recipe specifications. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Prepare ingredients for use in recipes for both hot and cold food production</li><li>Read recipes and prepare to specifications</li><li>Assist with set up, service, and clean-up of food serving line</li><li>Follow appropriate food handling and storage procedures</li><li>Serve food in serving line while adhering to portion control and serving procedures</li><li>Monitor and record refrigerator or freezer temperature readings</li><li>Assist with cold food production and assembly for catering functions</li><li>Operate cold food prep equipment</li><li>Provide routine and thorough cleaning of storage, cooking, serving, holding, dispensing equipment, and area. Empty trash. Assist in keeping the dining rooms neat and clean</li><li>Adhere to safety and sanitation guidelines, including related documentation</li><li>May operate computerized board checking system and perform other cash transactions</li><li>May assist in customer service functions</li></ul><div><br><strong>The work schedule for this position will be 12:30pm - 8:30pm Monday, Tuesday, and Friday and 12:00pm-8:00pm on Saturday and Sunday, with Wednesday and Thursday off.</strong></div><div><br><strong>Compensation:</strong></div><ul><li>The pay rate for this position is $19.65 per hour, and this role is eligible for overtime and shift/weekend differential</li><li>Shift Differentials: 10% for 2nd shift, 15% for 3rd shift, plus an additional $1.00/hour for weekend hours</li></ul><div><strong><br>Benefits and Perks:</strong></div><ul><li>Medical Insurance (Effective on date of hire)</li><li>Vision and Dental Insurance</li><li>Life Insurance and Disability Insurance</li><li>$1,000 Employee Referral Program Bonus</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 10.12% annual compensation contribution (Eligible after 1 year of service and age 26 )</li><li>Accrue up to 10 day of vacation (1st year), 15 days (2nd year)</li><li>Accrue up to 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>17 Paid Holidays</li><li>Paid Parental Leave (After 1 year)</li><li>Access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool (Including household)</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Dining Service - Thorne Hall https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18350 2026-09-04T14:44:19-04:00 2026-09-04T14:44:19-04:00 Budget and Financial Analyst <div>The Budget and Financial Analyst is an integral part of the College’s financial planning and budgeting team, working closely with the Vice President for Finance and Administration and Assistant Treasurer to support the institution’s long-term financial health and strategic goals. The position leads key budgeting, forecasting, financial analysis, and reporting activities, using Workday Financial Management and Workday Adaptive Planning to help inform decision-making. Serving as a valued partner to budget managers and departments, this individual provides guidance on budgeting, expenditures, and the effective use of operating, gift, and endowment funds. The role also assists with the annual budget process, and helps improve budget planning tools and processes. Success in this position requires strong analytical and problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and the ability to communicate financial information in a clear and approachable way. If you enjoy collaborating with colleagues, translating data into meaningful insights, and helping an organization achieve its goals, this is an excellent opportunity to make a significant impact.<br><br>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS</div><ul><li>Participates in all aspects of the budget process including draft budget presentations for senior officer discussions, preliminary Board budget presentations, drafting sections of the annual operating budget and other associated activities.&nbsp;</li><li>Partner with the Controller’s Office to ensure the accurate integration and reconciliation of budget data between Workday Financial Management and Workday Adaptive Planning.</li><li>Planning for budget to actual variance analysis, year-to-year budget changes, budget forecasting, scenario analysis, and other ad hoc analyses as needed.&nbsp;</li><li>Campus resource for majority of spending questions by campus community members, including the appropriate spending of operating budgets, gift funds, endowment funds, and all other types of spending.&nbsp;</li><li>Reviewing and approving (with input of VP Finance and Administration and Assistant Treasurer as appropriate) all budget change requests and journal entries.&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $95,000 - $105,000 annually.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div>BENEFITS AND PERKS&nbsp;</div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental) &nbsp;</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)&nbsp;</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance&nbsp;</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time &nbsp;</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a> &nbsp;</li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)&nbsp;</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool &nbsp;</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!&nbsp;</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a> &nbsp;</li></ul> Treasurers Office https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18110 2026-07-28T14:45:34-04:00 2026-07-28T14:45:35-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor of Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies (LACLaS) Program at Bowdoin College invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in migration and border studies at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a social or data scientist with a demonstrated interdisciplinary approach to artificial intelligence and immigration and border policies impacting U.S. Latinx, Caribbean, and/or Latin America who will engage students in the technological, ethical, political, and/or social landscapes that intertwine these studies. The teaching load is two courses per semester, teaching across the curriculum, and participating in the teaching rotation of the program’s intro course and LACLaS major requirements in the social sciences. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research, as well as evidence of how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 2) a curriculum vitae; and 3) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 10th</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually and at the associate professor rank is $120,000 - $140,000. The salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18335 2026-09-04T13:14:49-04:00 2026-09-04T13:14:50-04:00 Procurement & Risk Manager <div>The Procurement &amp; Risk Manager is responsible for managing the College’s property and casualty insurance programs to protect Bowdoin from operating and financial risks, and for providing strategic direction and implementing programs and processes related to College-wide procurement of goods and services. This role serves as a key advisor to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration, partnering across the institution to strengthen risk controls, improve purchasing practices, and support efficient, compliant operations. The position coordinates with internal stakeholders and external partners—including brokers, insurers, vendors, and counsel—to deliver measurable value, manage exposure, and enhance service levels.<br><br>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:</div><ul><li>Oversee the annual applications for insurance and renewal applications, conduct analysis to identify major causes and sources of risk losses and develop recommendations for strategic actions.</li><li>Provide assistance and support to Student Affairs regarding the procurement of student health insurance, sports/clubs/intermural insurance, and student health claims administration.</li><li>Establish bidding processes for potential vendors and negotiate prices and discounts, maintain relationships with vendors, provide estimates, and evaluate vendor credit history to ensure financial viability.</li><li>Oversee the coordination of providing information to claimants, College representatives, adjusters, attorneys and insurance companies.</li><li>Coordinate and conduct campus-wide risk management training sessions, guidelines, and procedures for all employees.</li><li>Collaborate with General Counsel to ensure that all legal contract requirements are met.</li></ul><div><br><br>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $124,000 - $140,000 annually.<br><br></div><div>BENEFITS AND PERKS</div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Treasurers Office https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18155 2026-08-07T12:42:56-04:00 2026-08-07T12:42:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Physics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Physics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek an experimental condensed-matter physicist who can actively involve undergraduate students in their research program. The teaching load is four courses a year. A Ph.D. in Physics is expected by the date of the appointment. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 1st</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Physics and Astronomy https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18337 2026-09-04T13:15:38-04:00 2026-09-04T13:15:38-04:00 Senior Accountant <div>The Senior Accountant has custodial responsibility for capital and non-capital project accounting, including project setup in the ERP system, security access management, funding allocations, and capitalization determinations. This role oversees key plant and project finance processes such as the monthly Plant Funding Analysis, reserve fund reporting, bond requisitions and related funding entries, and fixed asset accounting (capitalization and depreciation). The Senior Accountant prepares audit-ready schedules and documentation and serves as a primary resource in support of the annual financial statement audit. The position produces and coordinates required internal and external reports, surveys, and filings. In partnership with campus stakeholders, the Senior Accountant reviews and approves journal entries and budget override requests, resolves budget-check issues, and provides guidance on general accounting and compliance questions.<br><br>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS</div><ul><li>Provide stewardship for capital project accounting, including setting up capital project worktags in Workday and assigning appropriate security access for project managers and financial analysts. Maintain the monthly Plant Funding Analysis tracking each project’s budget, expenditures, funding sources, and funding status. Prepare monthly journal entries to fund project costs from gifts, reserves, and bond proceeds.</li><li>Manage the fixed asset ledger, including reviewing eligible expenditures, preparing capitalization and depreciation entries, and producing related audit schedules. Develop ad hoc analyses and reports as needed (e.g., depreciation projections and average age of plant).</li><li>Oversee non-capital project accounting, including establishing new projects and assigning security access for project managers and financial analysts. Build and maintain revenue-based budget rules and monitor/resolve budget override requests. Reconcile budget availability issues between Workday reporting and actual project balances, and resolve budget-check holds impacting overdue expense reports.</li><li>Prepare and coordinate required internal/external reporting and surveys, including the annual Welfare Benefit Plan income statement and related tax return data, Business Interruption worksheets, and institutional survey support. Prepare the monthly Reserve Funds Report.</li><li>Collaborate with the Vice President for Finance on bond-related activity, including reviewing proposed bond funding, compiling bond requisition support, and processing associated funding entries.</li><li>Review and approve journal entries submitted by campus partners, providing guidance on general accounting practices and collaborating to troubleshoot and resolve accounting and compliance issues.</li></ul><div><br><br>The hiring range for this position is expected to be: $85,000 - 95,000 annually.<br><br>BENEFITS AND PERKS</div><ul><li>A variety of health insurance plans (Medical, Vision, Dental)</li><li>Generous Retirement Plan – 401(a) and 403(b)</li><li>Life and Disability Insurance</li><li>Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per calendar year, 12 days of personal/sick time</li><li>Paid Holidays and Special Days Off: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/our-workplace/college-holidays-and-special-days-off.html</strong></a></li><li>Paid Parental Leave (Available after one year of service)</li><li>Household access to many of the College’s facilities including the gym and pool</li><li>Free fitness and wellness classes!</li><li>And more: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/hr/benefits-perks/index.html</strong></a></li></ul> Controllers Office https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18277 2026-08-25T09:24:26-04:00 2026-08-25T09:24:26-04:00 Assistant Professor of Dance <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Theater and Dance invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Dance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is contemporary modern dance with preference given to candidates who also offer an additional technique, especially one that expands our curricular offerings beyond the traditional Euro-American canon. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching who show promise of ongoing and impactful creative work. The successful candidate will have a strong technique and studio teaching practice and the ability to make technique accessible to students of all levels, mentor student choreographers, and set original work on students each semester. Candidates whose courses may cross-list with other campus departments and/or programs are especially encouraged to apply. An MFA in Dance is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for creative work with links to two samples of choreography not exceeding four-minutes combined; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references of candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 14, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Theater and Dance https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18339 2026-09-04T13:21:12-04:00 2026-09-04T13:21:13-04:00 Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns <div>In partnership with Lindauer, Bowdoin College is seeking a Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns for its extraordinary Development and Alumni Relations team.<br>Reporting to the Senior Vice President for Development and Alumni Relations, this leader will serve<br>as a strategic advisor, operational partner, and connective force for a division of nearly 60<br>professionals. They will be responsible for leading campaign management for Bowdoin’s upcoming<br>comprehensive campaign as well as future institutional priorities.<br><br>The successful candidate will bring significant fundraising and campaign experience, strong<br>judgment, and the ability to build trust and create clarity in a complex, fast-moving environment.<br>Bowdoin offers an experienced advancement leader the opportunity to build the structures and<br>partnerships that will turn ambitious institutional priorities into lasting impact.<br><br><em>The salary range for this position is $240,000–$260,000 annually.</em><br><br>To learn more, apply, or nominate a candidate, please visit:<br><a href=\"https://lindauerglobal.co/BowdoinChiefOfStaff\"><strong>https://lindauerglobal.co/BowdoinChiefOfStaff</strong></a></div> Development Administration https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18280 2026-08-25T09:25:15-04:00 2026-08-25T09:25:16-04:00 Assistant Professor of Philosophy <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Philosophy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in the philosophy of artificial intelligence (AI) at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is open, with a preference for candidates whose research involves AI related issues in applied ethics or who consider AI from the angle of the philosophy of cognitive science and the mind. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research or creative work. A Ph.D. in Philosophy is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this one, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your research plans; 4) a writing sample; 5) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Philosophy"
