    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/search.atom?utf8=%E2%9C%93&query=&query_v0_posted_at_date=&435=&query_position_type_id%5B%5D=2&commit=Search": {
      "title": "Bowdoin College: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:careers.bowdoin.edu,2005:/postings/search Bowdoin College: All Jobs 2026-09-04T15:33:51-04:00 https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18351 2026-09-04T15:33:51-04:00 2026-09-04T15:33:51-04:00 Assistant Professor of Mathematics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Mathematics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of assistant professor, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a candidate specializing in probability and stochastic processes, with a preference for those whose scholarship or teaching connects to the mathematics of artificial intelligence and machine learning. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in mathematics, applied mathematics, or statistics is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.</div><div><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.</div><div><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions through MathJobs (<a href=\"https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670</strong></a>). A complete application includes:</div><ul><li>a cover letter of up to two pages describing your experience and your short- and long-term goals in teaching and research. In your letter, please give specific examples of how your scholarship or teaching has engaged meaningfully with the mathematics underlying machine learning or AI – for example, stochastic optimization and sampling algorithms, high dimensional probability, diffusion models, statistical learning theory or teaching courses on the mathematical foundations of ML;</li><li>a curriculum vitae;</li><li>a research statement;</li><li>a teaching statement describing your pedagocial experience and your approach to engaging and supporting students from a broad range of backgrounds;</li><li>three letters of reference: two addressing research and one addressing teaching, submitted directly by the letter writers through MathJobs.</li></ul><div><br>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 8</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000-$98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.</div><div><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Mathematics https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18328 2026-09-03T15:17:31-04:00 2026-09-03T15:17:31-04:00 Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies (AI) <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in comparative public policy or governance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose research involves the law or regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) or the use of AI in policy-making; comparative research across countries or policy areas is a plus. The successful candidate will teach two courses per semester across a range of offerings, including participation in the rotation of the department’s introductory course in comparative politics or international relations. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in political science or related fields is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions – including this position - across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create inclusive learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 4) a writing sample; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 21, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<strong><br></strong><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Government https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18327 2026-09-03T15:17:05-04:00 2026-09-03T15:17:06-04:00 Assistant Professor of Government and Legal Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Government and Legal Studies invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the Assistant Professor level in the comparative politics of Africa. The position will begin July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach two courses per semester across a range of offerings, including the department’s introductory course in comparative politics, taught in rotation. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in political science is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create inclusive learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 4) a writing sample; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 21 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.</div><div><br>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Government https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18298 2026-08-28T10:30:24-04:00 2026-08-28T10:30:25-04:00 Lecturer in Computer Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, benefits-eligible lecturer-track position as Lecturer in Computer Science beginning July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for four years, with the potential for recurring multi-year reappointments and eventual promotion to Senior Lecturer, contingent upon successful review and reappointment. The teaching load is five courses per year and is expected to include a regular suite of core introductory-level courses (e.g. <em>Intro to Computer Science, Data Structures</em>) as well as intermediate and advanced courses within the candidate’s area of expertise as opportunity and demand allow. As the primary focus for lecturer-track faculty is on teaching and pedagogy, the successful candidate will have a demonstrated history of pedagogical innovation and a commitment to keep abreast of advances in computer science pedagogy. An advanced degree (master’s or doctorate) in Computer Science or a related field is expected by the date of appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching. The College offers opportunities for professional development, including a path to promotion to senior lecturer and eligibility for fully funded, one-semester senior lecturer sabbatical leaves, as well as support for teaching, grant-writing, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty, and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 4) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin<strong> January 19, 2027</strong>, and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment without prior lecturer-track experience is $94,000 - $100,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Computer Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18289 2026-08-26T09:53:43-04:00 2026-08-26T09:53:44-04:00 Assistant Professor of Cinema Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Cinema Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Cinema Studies at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and either documentary studies or television studies. Applicants to the documentary track may be scholar-practitioners; applicants to the television track may have a primarily scholarly focus. In either case, we welcome research examining AI’s social, political, aesthetic, economic, or ethical dimensions within the relevant field. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research or creative work. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines, including this position; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission. computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 5) a sample of scholarly work no longer than 20 pages; 6) if relevant, a film or other creative work of no more than 20 minutes’ duration accompanied by a creator’s statement of no more than 500 words, made accessible via a link (including a password, if desired) embedded in the candidate’s cover letter; and 7) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 4, 2026 </strong>and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Cinema Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18280 2026-08-25T09:25:15-04:00 2026-08-25T09:25:16-04:00 Assistant Professor of Philosophy <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Philosophy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in the philosophy of artificial intelligence (AI) at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is open, with a preference for candidates whose research involves AI related issues in applied ethics or who consider AI from the angle of the philosophy of cognitive science and the mind. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research or creative work. A Ph.D. in Philosophy is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this one, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your research plans; 4) a writing sample; 5) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Philosophy https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18279 2026-08-25T09:24:55-04:00 2026-08-25T09:24:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Classics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Classics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in classics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is ancient Mediterranean archaeology, with a preference for candidates whose research involves interactions between Greek, Roman, and other peoples. We welcome interdisciplinary and nontraditional approaches to the study of classics. The teaching load is two courses per semester; successful candidates will contribute enthusiastically to the department’s Latin, Greek and Classics course offerings. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in classics, archaeology, or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></d