ace, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Classics https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18277 2026-08-25T09:24:26-04:00 2026-08-25T09:24:26-04:00 Assistant Professor of Dance <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Theater and Dance invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Dance at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is contemporary modern dance with preference given to candidates who also offer an additional technique, especially one that expands our curricular offerings beyond the traditional Euro-American canon. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching who show promise of ongoing and impactful creative work. The successful candidate will have a strong technique and studio teaching practice and the ability to make technique accessible to students of all levels, mentor student choreographers, and set original work on students each semester. Candidates whose courses may cross-list with other campus departments and/or programs are especially encouraged to apply. An MFA in Dance is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for creative work with links to two samples of choreography not exceeding four-minutes combined; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references of candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin September 14, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Theater and Dance https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18155 2026-08-07T12:42:56-04:00 2026-08-07T12:42:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Physics <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Physics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek an experimental condensed-matter physicist who can actively involve undergraduate students in their research program. The teaching load is four courses a year. A Ph.D. in Physics is expected by the date of the appointment. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 1st</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Physics and Astronomy https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18112 2026-07-28T14:51:13-04:00 2026-07-28T14:51:14-04:00 Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Environmental Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in environmental humanities at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The humanities field is open and we welcome candidates who bring diverse humanistic perspectives to environmental inquiry, but excludes history for which expertise already exists in the program. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with the promise of long-term successful research and/or creative work. The successful candidate will teach four courses per year, including a rotating teaching responsibility for an introductory interdisciplinary environmental studies course, an intermediate-level humanities core course and an advanced-level capstone for environmental studies majors, and courses in the environmental humanities informed by the candidate’s area(s) of expertise. The successful candidate also is expected to direct student research.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research and/or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Environmental Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18110 2026-07-28T14:45:34-04:00 2026-07-28T14:45:35-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor of Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies (LACLaS) Program at Bowdoin College invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in migration and border studies at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a social or data scientist with a demonstrated interdisciplinary approach to artificial intelligence and immigration and border policies impacting U.S. Latinx, Caribbean, and/or Latin America who will engage students in the technological, ethical, political, and/or social landscapes that intertwine these studies. The teaching load is two courses per semester, teaching across the curriculum, and participating in the teaching rotation of the program’s intro course and LACLaS major requirements in the social sciences. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. is expected by the date of the appointment.</div><div><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter that includes a description of your research, as well as evidence of how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 2) a curriculum vitae; and 3) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 10th</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually and at the associate professor rank is $120,000 - $140,000. The salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Latin American, Caribbean, and Latinx Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18108 2026-07-28T14:42:26-04:00 2026-07-28T14:42:26-04:00 Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Earth and Oceanographic Science invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in geoscience applications of artificial intelligence at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose scholarship critically examines, thoughtfully utilizes, or ethically guides AI to advance understanding of geoscience processes. Areas of geoscience expertise might include glacial geology/geomorphology, glaciology, geophysics, neotectonics, sedimentology, stratigraphy, tectonic geomorphology, or atmospheric science, with a preference for those whose work intersects with surface earth processes and focuses on thousand- to million-year timescales. These fields and timescales have critical intersections with and implications for how humans live on and with Earth, even as the landscape and climate change in response to both natural and human activities. These areas of geoscience expertise also align with the EOS Department's earth system science approach to investigating fundamental questions about Earth’s past, present, and future.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will teach three courses per year, including two courses with separate lab sections. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term, successful scholarship and who will offer opportunities to engage students in research. A Ph.D. in geoscience or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this one, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.<br><br></div><div>The College’s location along the rocky Maine coast provides excellent local field sites for teaching and research. Bowdoin maintains a High Performance Computer (HPC) cluster and access to GIS software. Department facilities include mineral, rock, and fossil collections; augmented reality sandbox; stream table; rock saws; shallow water current meters; remote water samplers for river analysis; ACDP; petrographic microscopes; and SEM (Scanning Electron Microscope) with CL/EDS/EBSD capabilities. For more information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/earth-oceanographicscience/\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/earth-oceanographicscience/</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Pleasesubmit the following: (1) a one-page cover letter; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a three-page statement that describes your teaching practices, including a description of courses you would be interested in teaching that would enrich existing curriculum in EOS (<a href=\"https://bowdoin-public.courseleaf.com/courses/eos/\"><strong>https://bowdoin-public.courseleaf.com/courses/eos/</strong></a>); (4) a two-page research statement; (5) a one-page statement that describes your philosophy and use of AI; and (6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references for candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 1, 2026,</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.</div> Earth and Oceanographic Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18107 2026-07-28T14:39:02-04:00 2026-07-28T14:39:02-04:00 Assistant Professor of English (Creative Writing) <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of English invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in creative writing at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The subfields for this position are poetry and fiction, with a primary specialization in poetry and a secondary specialization in fiction. Successful candidates will have a strong record of publication and teaching in both subfields. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful creative work. An MFA, Ph.D., or equivalent terminal graduate degree in creative writing or a related discipline is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; 5) a writing sample of no more than 50 pages total that includes both fiction and poetry and 6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin Friday, <strong>September 18</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> English https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18104 2026-07-28T14:30:56-04:00 2026-07-28T14:30:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Computer Science <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Computer Science at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose research involves artificial intelligence (AI) or interdisciplinary work involving AI. We especially encourage those whose work intersects with trustworthy AI (e.g., explainability, interpretability, or privacy in AI models) or natural language processing (NLP) to apply. The teaching load is two courses per semester. This hire will teach at all levels of the Computer Science curriculum, including introductory courses as well as advanced courses within the candidate's area of expertise.&nbsp; Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this position, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of your plans for research 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Review of applications will begin October 1 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $122,000 - $128,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website:&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Computer Science https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18102 2026-07-28T14:16:45-04:00 2026-07-28T14:16:46-04:00 Assistant Professor of Asian Studies <div>Bowdoin College’s Asian Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Chinese language, literature and culture at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The area of specialization is open. The teaching load is two courses per semester including both language courses and thematic courses taught in English. The successful candidate will be integral in the Chinese language program, participating fully in the language program activities and teaching one to two courses in Chinese each year. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. Candidates must have native or near-native fluency in Mandarin and training in Chinese language pedagogy. A Ph.D is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and from those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College:<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please visit <a href=\"https://careers.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>https://careers.bowdoin.edu</strong></a> to submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>October 1, 2026 </strong>and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> Asian Studies https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18087 2026-07-27T14:53:41-04:00 2026-07-27T14:53:41-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor of Education <div>Bowdoin College’s Department of Education invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Education beginning July 1, 2027. Applicants at the Assistant and Associate level are encouraged to apply. The position subfield is open with a preference for candidates with a background in mathematics or data science and whose research involves Learning Sciences with a distinct focus on the development and role of artificial intelligence (AI) in teaching and learning. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in Education or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s Department of Education houses the <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/education/teacher-scholars/index.html\"><strong>Bowdoin Teacher Scholars</strong></a> (BTS) program that offers both current students and recent graduates the opportunity to become certified public school teachers. This hire will work in collaboration with current Education faculty to revise courses for the BTS pathway to include content related to AI.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin’s <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/hastings-ai-initiative/index.html\"><strong>Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity</strong></a> aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence.</div><div><br>Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks.<br><br></div><div>At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity.<br><br></div><div>Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: <a href=\"https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html\"><strong>https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html</strong></a>. In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available.<br><br></div><div>Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a description of your plans for research or creative work; 4) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 5) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references of candidates invited for interviews.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 15, 2026</strong> and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 - $98,000 annually and at the associate professor rank is $120,000 - $140,000. The salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate's experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check.<br><br></div><div>Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: <a href=\"http://www.bowdoin.edu/\"><strong>http://www.bowdoin.edu.</strong></a></div> Education"
    },
