partment of Philosophy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in the philosophy of artificial intelligence (AI) at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is open, with a preference for candidates whose research involves AI related issues in applied ethics or who consider AI from the angle of the philosophy ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Physics Physics and Astronomy Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Physics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek an experimental condensed-matter physicist who can actively involve undergraduate students in their research program. The teaching load is four courses a year. A Ph.D. in Physics is expected by th... View Details Bookmark Lecturer in Computer Science Computer Science Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, benefits-eligible lecturer-track position as Lecturer in Computer Science beginning July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for four years, with the potential for recurring multi-year reappointments and eventual promotion to Senior Lecturer, contingent upon successful review and reappointment. The teach... View Details Bookmark Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements