’s Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Physics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek an experimental condensed-matter physicist who can actively involve undergraduate students in their research program. The teaching load is four courses a year. A Ph.D. in Physics is expected by th... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Classics Classics Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Department of Classics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in classics at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. The position subfield is ancient Mediterranean archaeology, with a preference for candidates whose research involves interactions between Greek, Roman, and other peoples. We welcome interdisciplinary and nontradition... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Cinema Studies Cinema Studies Faculty Internal/External Bowdoin College’s Cinema Studies Program invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in Cinema Studies at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates working at the intersection of artificial intelligence and either documentary studies or television studies. Applicants to the documentary track may be scholar-practitioners; applicants to th... View Details Bookmark Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements